# The C fixtures the kernel's generic rung runs: each /mnt/tests/<name>.elf,
# expected to exit 42 (requests/d-a-one-rung-for-every-c-fixture.md).
# scripts/create-ext4-rootfs.sh stages this file at /tests/ctest-generic.list
# and refuses it if a line is malformed or names a fixture with no
# services/<name>/build.py.
#
# One fixture a line, three fields separated by blanks:
#
#   name      the fixture, services/<name>/: its ELF, and its argv[0]
#   grants    "-" for none, or a comma-separated list of kinds, each at
#             most once:
#               file   one wildcard File capability
#                      (READ | WRITE | EXECUTE | METADATA)
#               creds  (Process, SET_CREDENTIALS): set its own uid, gid and
#                      supplementary groups, as the fastpy-setuid rung grants
#             e.g. "file,creds"
#   seconds   how long it may take, from spawn to exit: 1 to 600
#
# and a fourth, for a fixture that runs a port only some worktrees build:
#
#   needs=<path>  what it runs, relative to the image's root: an image built
#             without it leaves the fixture off the staged list, with a
#             warning, rather than run it to fail every boot made from that
#             worktree (Opus's review of lane D's round 202)
#
# A fixture goes on only after it has passed in a lane D boot: none of
# another lane's boots should meet one of these failing for the first time.
#
# name           grants   seconds
ctest-obstack    -        30
ctest-argp       file     120
ctest-aio        file     30
ctest-cxx-throw  -        30
ctest-eintr      -        120
ctest-fortify-abort -        60
ctest-printf-streams -        30
ctest-pthread    -        120
ctest-stdio      file     60
ctest-sysvipc    -        30
ctest-ucontext   -        30
ctest-llvm-tools file     600  needs=bin/llc
ctest-sigpipe    -        30
ctest-rusage     -        60
ctest-pi-mutex   -        60
ctest-system     file     60
ctest-mmap-file  file     30
ctest-resuid     creds    30
ctest-groups     file,creds 30
ctest-fallocate  file     30
ctest-string     -        60
ctest-gdb-runs   file     300  needs=bin/gnu-gdb
ctest-mono-runs  file     300  needs=lib/mono/checks/checks.exe
ctest-binutils-runs file     300  needs=bin/as
ctest-gcc-runs   file     600  needs=usr/bin/gcc
ctest-unix-socket file     60
ctest-shared-anon -        30
ctest-cloexec-exec file     30
ctest-record-locks file     30
ctest-fsetfl-append file     60
ctest-positional-io file     60
ctest-timed-join -        30
ctest-sigign-exec file     30
ctest-renice     -        30
ctest-affinity   -        30
ctest-siginfo    -        30
ctest-tmpfile    file     30
ctest-seals      file     30
ctest-cpu-clocks -        60
ctest-itimers    -        60
ctest-posix-timers -      60
ctest-dumpable   file     30
ctest-thread-masks -        30
ctest-sigev-thread -        30
